## THE COMMISSION (RELAYED from the gate B906 verdict, read whole by the drafter; re-measure everything you rely on)
The product owner's 2026-10-29 ruling stands unchanged: roster before the skip list, one shared capture, no text changes. The gate went NO GO round 1 of 2 with a Blocker and three Majors that are all the fix's, plus two pinning gaps (STATUS `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-10-29_B906_STATUS.md`, FOR TUESDAY 227-269, FINDINGS 134-141, ADDENDUM-1 RESULTS 175-226; the builder report is `.../2026-10-29_B895_STATUS.md`). **Read both whole first.**
- **B906-1 Blocker.** `checkForCurrentUserQuery` now takes the FIRST candidate the roster stage OR the skip list accepts; base took the first BASE-VALID one. So a rostered skip-word account earlier in pattern order preempts the user base answered: "has admin printed less than when was the last time quokka wombat printed?" (roster `Admin`, `Quokka Wombat`): base answers Quokka Wombat, head answers Admin (437 pairs in the gate's census; reproduced on the real server). Same through a non-skip-list reject: "what did zq doe spend on toner last quarter?" (pattern 1 captures `zq`, which fails the name-like-word test; pattern 3 captures `zq doe`).
- **B906-2 Major.** The conjunct `matchRosterUsers(capture, rosterNames).length > 0` asks whether the resolver finds ANY roster name, not the strict-hit name: roster `Guest ` (trailing space) + `guest.house@example.invalid` makes "did guest print last week?" answer guest.house's activity; `Wombat  Guest` (two spaces) + `ann.wombat.guest@example.invalid` makes "how much has wombat guest printed?" answer ann.wombat.guest's (723 pairs).
- **B906-4 Major (fallback only).** "show me admin's activity", model endpoint down: base's sibling `(\w+)'s` answered Admin; pattern 4 of the shared list captures the leftmost "me admin", the pronoun-lead test rejects it, and the answer becomes the no-user text. True for every one-word user, not only skip words.
- **B906-6, B906-7 Major (pinning rows that cannot fail).** No cell holds the part-before-`@` arm or the dot collapse in `rosterKey`; the gate's mutants MP and MK stayed green. **B906-8 Minor:** no cell holds the resolver conjunct (MS). **B906-3 Note, folded here:** `matchRosterUsers` calls `name.toLowerCase()` on every roster value, so a non-string `User_Name` throws inside the capture.
- **Not in this lane:** B906-5 (failure-path comment), FINDING 1 (verb-led capture "has she", "did zq"), the cost Note: the records seat tickets them. Do not touch them. RD-872 stays open and pinned by the existing C4 cell.

